# WHAT EAS BUILD DOES NOT UPLOAD.
#
# EAS archives from the REPOSITORY ROOT (the build log shows the project at
# `/home/expo/workingdir/build/mobile`), so this file belongs here and its
# paths are repo-relative. When a .easignore exists it REPLACES .gitignore as
# the upload filter, so this is written as a deliberate superset of every
# ignore file in the repo — the root one, backend/.gitignore and the nested
# mobile/android/.gitignore.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS.
#
# The demo is built with EAS_NO_VCS=1, because `mobile/src/demo/` and
# `mobile/app.config.js` are untracked and a git-based upload would ship a
# build with the whole demo layer missing. In that mode the CLI does not
# honour NESTED ignore files, and `mobile/android/.gitignore` is the ONLY
# place `build/` is listed — the root .gitignore covers
# `android/app/build/` and `android/.gradle/` but not `android/build/`.
#
# So a local Windows build's `mobile/android/build/generated/autolinking/`
# was uploaded. React Native's settings plugin caches autolinking there and
# reuses it whenever the adjacent package.json.sha / package-lock.json.sha
# still match — which they did. The Linux builder therefore resolved
# react-native-gesture-handler, -safe-area-context, -screens, -svg and
# -webview at `C:\Users\...` paths that do not exist on it, and Gradle failed
# with "No matching variant ... No variants exist" for exactly those five.
#
# The mobile/android entries below are what prevent that recurring after any
# local `expo run:android`.

# ---- Dependencies. The builder runs `npm ci` itself. ----
node_modules/
mobile/node_modules/
backend/node_modules/

# ---- Secrets. The demo's only env var (EXPO_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE) comes from
#      the `demo` profile in eas.json, never from a file. ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
backend/.env

# ---- Not part of an Android build. `mobile-temp/` is a 319 MB scratch copy
#      of the app and `backend/` is the server; neither is compiled here. ----
mobile-temp/
backend/
database/

# ---- Expo / Metro ----
.expo/
.expo-shared/
dist/
web-build/
mobile/.tmp-rn/

# ---- NATIVE BUILD OUTPUT. All regenerated on the builder; uploading a local
#      machine's copy is what broke the two builds described above. ----
mobile/android/build/
mobile/android/.gradle/
mobile/android/.cxx/
mobile/android/app/build/
mobile/android/app/.cxx/
mobile/android/local.properties
mobile/android/.idea/
mobile/android/*.iml
mobile/android/*.hprof
mobile/ios/build/
mobile/ios/Pods/
*.jsbundle

# ---- Logs and OS noise ----
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
